# chapterwise — Cursor project rules

Textbook PDF → ordered topics (chapters/sections/subsections) + per-topic explanation, Q&A, images, and TTS narration.

**Monorepo layout:** `backend/` is a standalone FastAPI app (`python backend/main.py`). `frontend/` is a standalone Vite React app (`npm run dev` from `frontend/`). Do not mix Python and JS across folders. **`frontend/src/config/api.js` is the only place the backend base URL/port should be hardcoded** (default `http://127.0.0.1:8766`).

---

## 1. What this app does (v1 goal)

1. User uploads a textbook PDF.
2. Backend extracts text + images per page (local PyMuPDF + pdfplumber, or optional **Kaggle** remote extract via tunnel).
3. **Regex heading scan** (default) builds an **ordered** hierarchical topic tree (chapter → section → subsection) in document order. Optional legacy path: Kaggle Llama / Azure via `CHAPTERWISE_TOPIC_BUILDER=llm`.
4. Each topic shows explanation, source page range, and formula/diagram images from those pages.
5. User asks questions grounded in that topic’s text only.
6. User presses Listen for OpenAI TTS narration.

**Different from magazine/Veda app:** topics are **hierarchical** and stay in **document order** (not layout/font driven). Images attach to topics by page range.

---

## 2. Build order (§8) — status

| Step | Scope | Status |
|------|--------|--------|
| **1** | Backend `/upload_pdf` + `pdf_extract.py` (per-page text + images) | ✅ Done |
| **2** | Backend `/build_topics` + `topic_builder.py` (ordered tree; **regex default**, optional LLM) | 🟡 Partial — **regex TOC works** (full Class 9 Science 1299 pp → 223 topics / 214 headings in **0.16s**); title/order still OCR-noisy; **full-book false `Chapter N` hits** (duplicate/out-of-order chapter nodes); LLM path kept behind `CHAPTERWISE_TOPIC_BUILDER=llm` |
| **3** | Frontend `UploadPanel` + `TopicTree` wired to upload + build_topics | ✅ Done — wired; **sidebar inner-scrolls** (`.app-shell` `height: 100vh; overflow: hidden`; `.topic-tree-list` `flex:1; min-height:0; overflow: auto`) |
| **4** | Backend `/topic/{id}` + Frontend `TopicView` (explanation + image gallery) | 🟡 Partial — LLM explanation + Listen ✅; **deferred image b64** + on-demand encode; gallery **drops `isBackground`**; markdown explanation/answers; enhance wired (step 7) |
| **5** | Backend `/ask` + Frontend `AskPanel` (grounded Q&A) | ✅ Done — `qa.py` + `POST /ask` + `AskPanel` under explanation; refuse-to-guess prompt; no Q&A cache |
| **6** | Backend `/tts` + Listen button in `TopicView` | ✅ Done — `/tts` + Listen; default voice **`shimmer`** (female); narrates explanation (falls back to source text) |
| **7** | Backend `image_enhance.py` (informational → Lanczos, decorative → gpt-image-2) | 🟡 Partial — **wired**: cheap classify + baked-text OCR; informational → Lanczos; decorative → **on-demand** `POST .../generate` (gpt-image-2). `overlapWordCount` still **0 on RapidOCR extract path** (ignored as a gate). |
| **8** | End-to-end polish; revisit `# TODO v2` items | ⬜ Not started |

**When continuing work:** follow this order. Do one step at a time unless the user explicitly asks for multiple steps. Get user test approval between major steps when they ask for that workflow.

