## 6. Session updates & decisions (changelog)

- **Step 1:** Created backend with `/upload_pdf`, `pdf_extract.py`, `security.py`, debug extraction endpoints. Smoke-tested 90-page PDF.
- **Step 2:** Added `topic_builder.py`, `/build_topics`, `/debug/topics`. Azure OpenAI v1 API via standard `OpenAI` client + `base_url` + deployment name as `model=`.
- **Step 3:** Scaffolded Vite React frontend; `UploadPanel` + `TopicTree` + `DocContext` + `apiClient.js`.
- **PDF size limit:** Set to **500 MB** (`CHAPTERWISE_MAX_PDF_BYTES=524288000`).
- **`.env`:** Created `backend/.env` with Azure Foundry credentials (text, TTS, image deployments). Never commit `.env`.
- **Upload slowness (300 MB books):** Upload waits for **full local extraction** of every page before responding — not OpenAI. Discussed but not implemented: fast upload + background extraction, OpenAI/hybrid parsing for scanned PDFs.
- **Parallel extraction:** All CPU cores used locally; pdfplumber one open per page.
- **Kaggle remote extraction:** Bundle publish scripts, GPU notebook server, `kaggle_client.py`, `EXTRACT_PROVIDER` routing in `main.py`.
- **2026-07-24 — Kaggle large-PDF reliability:** Chunked upload (`/upload_chunk`), async extract with polling (`/extract/status`, `/extract/result`), poll retries. Published updated bundle to `eakeswar/chapterwise-models`. Tunnel URL must be refreshed in `.env` each notebook session.
- **2026-07-24 — Page-range extraction:** `extract_document()` + `/upload_pdf?page_start=&page_end=`; frontend “Test first pages only” now limits parse scope (full PDF still uploaded to Kaggle).
- **2026-07-24 — Azure topic build blocked:** API key + base URL for `edzhub-resource` work, but **`AZURE_TEXT_DEPLOYMENT=gpt-4o-mini` not deployed** → `DeploymentNotFound` on `/build_topics`. Need deployment created in Azure Foundry or new resource. API URLs are not browsable in Chrome (POST-only).
- **2026-07-27 — Azure deployment audit:** TTS (`gpt-4o-mini-tts`) and images (`gpt-image-2`) work on `https://edzhub-resource.services.ai.azure.com/openai/v1`. Chat (`gpt-4o-mini`) still `DeploymentNotFound` on `https://edzhub-resource.openai.azure.com/openai/v1`. Added `azure_clients.py`, `GET /debug/azure`, `POST /tts`, `tts.py`, basic `image_enhance.py`.
- **2026-07-27 — Step 4 shell:** `topic_detail.py`, `GET /topic/{topic_id}`, `TopicView.jsx` (source text + images, no LLM explanation yet), `topicCache`, shimmer skeletons, Listen button (TTS on source text).
- **2026-07-27 — Upload UX:** `UploadLoadingScreen.jsx` with animated progress bar + step labels during upload/build.
- **2026-07-27 — Kaggle tunnel refreshed:** `KAGGLE_API_BASE_URL=https://maiden-evaluate-ranked-short.trycloudflare.com` (ephemeral; update each notebook session). Verified reachable with 2 GPUs. Full PDF upload to Kaggle works; `/build_topics` still blocked by missing Azure chat deployment.
