- **2026-08-03 — Kaggle chat client fix:** `kaggle_client.py` — added `_post_json_with_retry()`; `kaggle_chat_completions()` was incorrectly passing `json=` to byte-upload `_post_with_retry()` → `name 'json' unexpected` / broken `/debug/text`.
- **2026-08-03 — Topic build fixes:** Removed dead `get_openai_client()` from `topic_builder.py`. Added JSON repair (trailing commas, unclosed brackets) + one automatic retry with “valid JSON only” follow-up for Llama 1B malformed output.
- **2026-08-03 — Kaggle ops (Class 9 Science textbook test, 301 MB / 1299 pages):** Full PDF still uploads to Kaggle even with “Test first pages only” (page range limits **extract** only). **`EXTRACT_PROVIDER=local`** recommended for laptop dev (skip 76-chunk Kaggle upload; ~3 min local extract for 15–20 pages). **`CHAPTERWISE_TOPIC_CHUNK_PAGES=8`** reduces Llama VRAM per chunk. **`KAGGLE_API_SECRET`** must match notebook cell 2 exactly (placeholder causes 401). **`HF_TOKEN`** + Hugging Face gated access required for Llama (“Expand to review and access” on model page; affiliation can be `Individual`). Set notebook `CHAPTERWISE_LLM_PRELOAD=1`, `CHAPTERWISE_LLM_4BIT=1`, lower `MAX_INPUT_CHARS` / `MAX_NEW_TOKENS` to avoid CUDA OOM on T4. Cloudflare tunnel dies mid-session (502 / error 1033) — refresh URL each notebook run. First successful `/debug/text` after preload: `"ok": true`, `"llm_loaded": true`. Sample born-digital NCERT-style PDF pages extract well with pdfplumber (no GPU OCR needed for v1).
- **2026-08-10 — Extract perf (header/footer):** `pdf_extract.py` header/footer scan was parsing all 1299 pages even for `page_start=1&page_end=10` (~93s of ~98s). Fixed: sample **36 evenly spaced pages** + cache by file fingerprint. Pages 1–10 local extract dropped to ~6–8s. Added `CHAPTERWISE_DEBUG_TIMING=1`. Laptop `CHAPTERWISE_TEXT_EXTRACTOR=rapidocr`, `CHAPTERWISE_RAPIDOCR_FORCE=0`.
- **2026-08-10 — Topic build OOM + tunnel 502:** Llama 1B on T4 OOM during `/chat/completions` when prompt + `max_new_tokens=4096` spiked attention (~13 GB). Pattern: first call often succeeds; **JSON retry** (bad output + full chunk) triggers CUDA OOM or Cloudflare **502 Bad gateway** (tunnel loses Kaggle mid-request). Fixes: `llm_server.py` — defaults `MAX_NEW_TOKENS=1024`, `MAX_INPUT_CHARS=12000`, truncate **all** messages to total budget, assistant cap 2000, `empty_cache()` after generate, `repetition_penalty=1.2`. `topic_builder.py` — retry assistant capped at `CHAPTERWISE_TOPIC_RETRY_CHARS=2000`. `main.py` — `/build_topics` uses `CHAPTERWISE_TOPIC_CHUNK_PAGES` from env (not hardcoded 18). Republished `eakeswar/chapterwise-models`. Topic prompt tightened (Activity rules, section limits, anti-leak example); sanity warnings for bad trees. Tree quality on Class 9 Science OCR still rough (fabricated subsections, parallel “chapters” for 1.1/1.2).
- **2026-08-11 — Kaggle secrets + HF auth:** Notebook cell 2 loads **`KAGGLE_API_SECRET`** and **`HF_TOKEN`** via `UserSecretsClient` (Add-ons → Secrets). Missing `HF_TOKEN` secret caused 401 gated-repo (not HF permissions). Missing/mismatched `KAGGLE_API_SECRET` caused laptop `401 Invalid or missing API token` on `/chat/completions` while `/health` still looked fine. `llm_server` prints `HF auth token present/len` before load; uses `token=` + `huggingface_hub.login`.
- **2026-08-11 — Async chat (tunnel 524):** Sync `/chat/completions` often exceeded Cloudflare free-tunnel ~100s → **524 A timeout occurred** even when Llama finished on Kaggle. Added Kaggle `POST /chat` + `GET /chat/status` + `GET /chat/result`; laptop `kaggle_client.kaggle_chat_completions()` polls like extract. Republished dataset. Prefer **Test first pages only = 8** and `CHAPTERWISE_TOPIC_CHUNK_PAGES=4` while validating. End-to-end build still needs user confirmation after attaching latest dataset version.
- **2026-08-12 — Kaggle chat reliability (Plan A):** Busy chat → 409 + `job_id`; client retries 409/502; no sync fallback except 404/405; generate `max_time` + StoppingCriteria; chat job watchdog + `/chat/reset`. Topic-sized Llama prompts (~12.5k chars) still hang on T4; tiny/medium chats OK (~2s).
- **2026-08-12 — Regex topic builder (Plan B):** Default `CHAPTERWISE_TOPIC_BUILDER=regex` — heading regex TOC, no Llama. Body text kept via page ranges (approach a); empty-range fallback chapter (approach b). Pages 1–8 Class 9 Science: ~21 topics in 0.01s. OCR title spill / two-column order issues documented; fix deferred pending user decision. LLM path: `CHAPTERWISE_TOPIC_BUILDER=llm`.
- **2026-08-13 — Regex TOC confirmed live:** `CHAPTERWISE_TOPIC_BUILDER` is often **unset** in `.env` (code default `regex`, not leftover `llm`). Pages 1–8 Class 9 Science: `POST /build_topics` → HTTP 200, `builder=regex`, `heading_count=20`, `topic_count=21` in ~0s. `GET /debug/topics` populated. OCR title spill still present (`Matter of sa`, truncated titles, `1.4.1 EFFECT` before `1.4`).
- **2026-08-13 — Dead Kaggle must not block `/topic`:** With `TEXT_PROVIDER=kaggle` and a dead tunnel, `GET /topic/{id}` hung until `CHAPTERWISE_LLM_TIMEOUT` (600s) because `_kaggle_start_chat_job` retried DNS/connection errors in a loop. **Fix:** after `_post_json_with_retry` exhausts retries, raise `Kaggle chat unreachable` immediately. `topic_detail` still returns HTTP 200 with `explanation_status=failed`, source text + images (~3s). UI already shows the failed-explanation notice.
- **2026-08-13 — Azure chat on a separate resource:** New Foundry resource `chapterwise-text` (user’s account). Chat uses **`AZURE_CHAT_API_KEY`** + **`AZURE_CHAT_BASE_URL`** (must include `/openai/v1`). TTS/images keep `AZURE_OPENAI_API_KEY` + services endpoint. Laptop `TEXT_PROVIDER=azure`, `AZURE_TEXT_DEPLOYMENT=gpt-4.1-mini`. Missing `/openai/v1` on the chat URL → 404 Resource not found.
- **2026-08-13 — Extract/TOC stay local:** Kaggle T4 GPUs run **Llama only**; PyMuPDF/RapidOCR + regex TOC are CPU. Do not move extract or regex tree to Kaggle to “use the 2 GPUs.” Optional later: Kaggle CPU extract + regex colocation to avoid pulling full extract JSON through the tunnel (`topic_builder.py` is not in the Kaggle dataset bundle yet).
- **2026-08-14 — Full-book local extract:** Class 9 Science 301 MB / 1299 pages, `EXTRACT_PROVIDER=local`, RapidOCR, 16 thread workers. First run (eager b64, RapidOCR init race): **286.91s** extract, peak private **~2.44 GB**. After defer-b64 + single RapidOCR init: **~209s** extract on a later full run. `images_extract_encode` timing still includes `get_images`/`get_image_rects` even when b64 is deferred.
- **2026-08-14 — Defer image b64 locally + RapidOCR init lock:** `main.py` `os.environ.setdefault("CHAPTERWISE_DEFER_IMAGE_B64", "1")` after `.env` load (`.env` can still set `0`). `_get_rapidocr_pdf()` constructs `RapidOCRPDF` once under `_RAPIDOCR_LOCK`.
- **2026-08-14 — On-demand image encode:** `GET /topic/{id}` hydrates missing `url`s via `encode_xref_data_url()` for that topic’s xrefs only; in-memory cache `{pdf fingerprint}:{xref}`. `jpx`/`jp2`/etc. converted to PNG (Separation/CMYK pixmaps go through RGB). Gallery **excludes `isBackground`** (page-2 Activity 1.3/1.4/1.5 duplicate galleries were only backgrounds). Images still attach by **page range only**; heading `start` char offsets are dropped after TOC build. Same-page sibling non-bg sharing still exists but is rare on pp.1–8 (e.g. one figure on p.3 shared by Activity 1.6/1.7/1.8). Position-based split **not built**.
- **2026-08-14 — Step 5 Q&A:** `qa.py` `answer_question()` + `POST /ask` `{ topic_id, question }`. Context = cached explanation (if any) + page-range source. System prompt: answer only from context, else say this section does not have enough information. HTTP 200 + `status=failed` on provider error (same fail-fast as `/topic`). `AskPanel` in `TopicView`. Smoke: Activity 1.1 → “Panch Tatva”; boiling point of water refused.
- **2026-08-14 — Full-book TOC + UI:** `/build_topics` on 1299 pp → **223 topics / 214 headings / 0.16s**. Regex false `Chapter N` matches → 37 chapter nodes, duplicate/out-of-order titles (e.g. several “Chapter 6”, last “Chapter 8” at pp.1290–1299 is likely answers/appendix). Start/mid/end `/topic` + `/ask` + Listen worked (Activity 1.1 p.1, Activity 8.4 p.650, ch37 pp.1290–1299). TTS default voice **`shimmer`**.
- **2026-08-14 — TTS voice:** `tts.py` `DEFAULT_VOICE = "shimmer"` (female). Listen does not pass `voice`, so this default applies. Restart backend after the change (clears in-memory extract).
- **2026-08-17 — Black gallery images (SMask):** Page-1-style 1-bit ICC Gray + **SMask** decoded as raw PNG looked solid black (artwork in the mask). `encode_xref_data_url()` now Pixmap-decodes unsafe/SMask/low-bpc/CMYK/Separation images to RGB PNG with mask as alpha.
- **2026-08-17 — Step 7 on-demand generate:** `/topic` Lanczos for informational+low quality; decorative stays original unless cache already has `kind=generated`. **`POST /topic/{id}/images/{image_id}/generate`** — 400 if not decorative (`InformationalImageError`); Azure/timeout → HTTP 200 `{status: failed}`. Size `1024x1024`. Gallery: Generate HD / Show original. Do **not** auto-run gpt-image-2 on topic open (pages with many decorative images, e.g. p174).
- **2026-08-17 — Generate prompt must follow the photo:** Vision caption describes **only** the attached pixels (no topic). gpt-image-2 prompt: redraw that caption; topic title is **style only**. Negatives: no people/vehicles/animals/tools not in the caption. Including chapter explanation as subject turned “wheat grains” (p684) into a farm scene when generated from **`ch20` (Chapter 12)** instead of `ch20_s1_ss1`.
- **2026-08-17 — Baked-in diagram labels:** Color labeled figures (p68 `p68_i0` XYLEM / `p68_i1` PHLOEM) classified decorative because overlap=0, aspect below 2.2, chroma above 25. Labels are **raster pixels**, not PDF text. **RapidOCR on the cropped image** (lazy, background, max side 512): at least one string (score ≥ 0.5, length ≥ 2) → force informational + Lanczos; photos like p684 wheat stay decorative. Eager full-book OCR is hours — **do not** run OCR on every extract image.
- **2026-08-17 — Classify must not block `/topic`:** Would-be-decorative tiles return `classify_status=pending`, `enhance_role=informational` (Generate HD **blocked** until OCR finishes — fail conservative). 2-worker pool; cache by source hash. `TopicView` polls `/topic` every 3s. Cheap informational (wide aspect / gray line-art) skips OCR.
- **2026-08-17 — Frontend polish:** `react-markdown` via `MarkdownText.jsx` for explanation + Ask answers (TTS still plain text). Topic tree viewport scroll (see §5). `/build_topics` page range uses **extracted PDF page numbers** so a 172–176 slice is not remapped to “Pages 1–5”.
- **2026-08-19 — Changelog/rules sync:** Audited staged (uncommitted) code vs `.cursorrules`. Feature work above landed **2026-08-14–17**; tonight’s diff is documentation alignment only — §2 build-order table, §4 endpoints/state, §5 frontend, §9 step-7 checklist, §11 known issues, §12 next steps. Staged files: `image_enhance.py`, `pdf_extract.py`, `topic_detail.py`, `main.py`, `topic_builder.py`, `TopicView.jsx`, `MarkdownText.jsx`, `AskPanel.jsx`, `index.css`, `api.js` / `apiClient.js`, `package.json`, `.gitignore` (test_output samples).

