## 8. Explicit non-goals for v1 (flag as `# TODO v2`)

- No **Azure** chat fallback when `TEXT_PROVIDER=kaggle` — if Kaggle text is selected, do not silently use the TTS/image key for chat. Current default is `TEXT_PROVIDER=azure` (separate `AZURE_CHAT_*` creds); TTS/images stay on the edzhub services endpoint.
- No karaoke word highlighting — play/pause audio per topic only
- No image **generation** for formula/diagram images — Lanczos upscale only for informational images; `gpt-image-2` only for small/blurry **decorative** images (step 7)
- No multi-user auth — single active document
- No vector DB — topic Q&A uses raw topic text in prompt context
- No disk caching — in-memory only
- No OpenAI for full-book PDF parsing (local extract first; hybrid vision fallback is v2)

---

## 9. Remaining implementation notes (steps 4–7)

### `/topic/{topic_id}` + `TopicView`

- ✅ Join topic node from `topics_by_id` with page-range slice of `_active_extraction`
- ✅ Source text + image gallery in `TopicView`
- ✅ LLM explanation via `text_provider.chat_completion` in `topic_detail.py` (`explanation_status`: ready | skipped | failed)
- ✅ Listen button via `POST /tts` (narrates explanation, falls back to source text)
- ✅ Deferred extract b64; `/topic` encodes on demand; gallery skips `isBackground`
- ✅ Images run through `image_enhance.py` on `/topic` (cheap classify + background baked-text OCR; Lanczos for informational+low quality)
- ✅ On-demand decorative generate: `POST /topic/{id}/images/{image_id}/generate`
- ⬜ Optional: assign non-bg images to same-page sibling topics via heading offset vs image `y` (deferred — rare on Class 9 pp.1–8)
- `# TODO v2`: richer formula vs decorative classification; compute `overlapWordCount` on RapidOCR extract path (PyMuPDF words) if we want overlap as an informational shortcut again

### `/ask` + `AskPanel`

- ✅ `qa.py` + `POST /ask` + `AskPanel` (explanation + source in context; refuse outside topic)
- ⬜ No Q&A cache (v1: every question is a fresh call)

### `/tts` + Listen

- ✅ `tts.py` + `POST /tts` on `AZURE_TTS_BASE_URL` (services endpoint)
- ✅ Listen button in `TopicView` (explanation text, fallback to source text)
- ✅ Default voice **`shimmer`**
- ⬜ Optional: `POST /tts` with `{ topic_id }` after explanation exists

### `image_enhance.py` (§4a)

- ✅ `generate_decorative_image()` via `gpt-image-2` (size `1024x1024`)
- ✅ Cheap classify: aspect ≥ 2.2 or gray/line-art (mean chroma under 25) → informational. **`overlapWordCount` is not a gate** (RapidOCR extract always stores 0).
- ✅ Baked-text OCR (RapidOCR on image pixels, downscaled max 512): if would-be decorative, run **in background**; ≥1 decent string → informational. Until `classify_status=ready`, treat as informational (no Generate HD).
- ✅ Quality: small (`SMALL_IMAGE_MIN_DIM=400`) or blurry (Laplacian under `BLUR_VARIANCE_THRESHOLD=100`)
- ✅ Route: informational + low quality → **Lanczos**; decorative → original until user **Generate HD** (never gpt-image-2 formulas/diagrams)
- ✅ Prompt: vision describes the photo only; generate prompt is caption-primary + style from topic **title** only (no explanation dump)
- ✅ In-memory `_ENHANCE_CACHE` keyed by source SHA-256 (includes classify result; decorative originals are cached so OCR does not rerun)
- Do **not** auto-generate decorative images on `/topic` (too many per page; Azure cost + latency)

---

## 10. Coding preferences

- Python 3.11+, FastAPI, async where possible
- pip installs → `backend/vendor/` via `--target`
- Print logging OK for v1
- **Ask for approval before editing existing files** unless the user explicitly says to proceed/build/implement
- Never commit `backend/.env`, `backend/vendor/`, `backend/active_doc.pdf`
- Never hardcode API keys in source
- Keep changes scoped; match existing style
- Frontend: minimal CSS (no Tailwind in chapterwise v1), functional components only

---

## 11. Known issues & ops

- **Text/chat:** Default `TEXT_PROVIDER=azure` uses `AZURE_CHAT_API_KEY` + `AZURE_CHAT_BASE_URL` + `AZURE_TEXT_DEPLOYMENT=gpt-4.1-mini`. Verify with `GET /debug/text`. `TEXT_PROVIDER=kaggle` uses Kaggle async `/chat` (poll); `auto` falls back to Azure if Kaggle text fails. Dead Kaggle must fail fast (not spin until `CHAPTERWISE_LLM_TIMEOUT`) so `/topic` still returns source + images.
- **Azure TTS/images:** Still `AZURE_OPENAI_API_KEY` on `services.ai.azure.com`. Verify with `GET /debug/azure`. Default TTS voice is **`shimmer`**. Do not send chat requests with the TTS/image key.
- **Azure chat URL:** `AZURE_CHAT_BASE_URL` **must include `/openai/v1`**. Host-only URL → 404 Resource not found. Restart backend after `.env` edits.
- **Kaggle tunnel:** Free `trycloudflare.com` URLs are ephemeral — refresh `KAGGLE_API_BASE_URL` each notebook run. **`/health` is fast and unauthenticated**. Long sync `/chat/completions` can fail with **524** (timeout) or **502**; use async `/chat` polling on latest dataset. `KAGGLE_API_SECRET` must **exactly match** notebook UserSecrets (placeholder/`PASTE_…` → 401 on chat). Prefer **`EXTRACT_PROVIDER=local`** for fast dev; use `auto` or `kaggle` for full offloaded extract.
- **Kaggle Llama gated model:** Accept license on https://huggingface.co/meta-llama/Llama-3.2-1B-Instruct (“Expand to review and access”); set `HF_TOKEN` via Kaggle Add-ons → Secrets. 401 with `present=False` → secret not loaded; 401 with `present=True` → HF access not granted for that token’s account.
- **Kaggle Llama runtime:** Use `CHAPTERWISE_LLM_PRELOAD=1`. CUDA OOM on T4 → `CHAPTERWISE_TOPIC_CHUNK_PAGES=4` or `8`, `CHAPTERWISE_LLM_MAX_INPUT_CHARS=12000`, `CHAPTERWISE_LLM_MAX_NEW_TOKENS=1024`, republish dataset after `llm_server.py` / `chapterwise_gpu_server.py` changes. Llama 1B may return malformed topic JSON → repair + retry in `topic_builder.py` (retry assistant capped at 2000 chars).
- **Large PDFs (e.g. 300 MB):** Browser sends full file to laptop every upload. “Test first pages only” limits **extract** page range, not upload size. Kaggle path uploads all 76×4 MB chunks before extract. Local **full-book** extract of Class 9 Science (1299 pp / 301 MB) ≈ **3.5 min** with defer-b64 + RapidOCR (was ~4.8 min with eager b64). Partial 15–20 pages ≈ 3–5 min was the old pdfplumber-era figure — RapidOCR + header-sample cache is much faster for small ranges (~6–8s for pp.1–10).
- **Full-book regex TOC:** 223 topics in 0.16s, but many false `Chapter N` headings (duplicate/out-of-order chapter nodes). Title spill / two-column OCR order still present on early pages.
- **`overlapWordCount` is unused on laptop RapidOCR extracts** (2732/2732 were 0 on Class 9 Science). Color diagrams with labels painted into the JPEG (p68 xylem/phloem) need baked-text OCR, not PDF overlap.
- **Generate HD from a chapter node** (`ch20` = whole Chapter 12) used to illustrate the **topic**, not the photo. Generate from the tight subsection when possible; prompt no longer injects explanation as subject.
- Only one upload/build at a time (`_extraction_lock`); backend blocks `/health` during active job
- **Port 8766 in use:** Stop prior `python backend/main.py` (Ctrl+C) before restarting
- Restart backend after `.env` changes; restart clears in-memory extraction/topics/explanations
- Frontend dev server: port **5173** — must be running separately (`npm run dev`)
- After Kaggle code changes: republish dataset + re-run notebook cells 1–2; copy new tunnel URL to `.env`
- Kaggle notebook pip warnings (`dopamine-rl`/`gym`, `gradio`/`pillow`) are harmless

---

## 12. Next step when user says “continue”

**Next:** (1) Tighten regex TOC for full-book false `Chapter N` hits / title spill / two-column order. (2) Optional: compute `overlapWordCount` on the RapidOCR extract path (PyMuPDF words vs image rects) as an extra informational shortcut. (3) Optional later: same-page non-bg image split by heading offset vs `y`. (4) `# TODO v2`: skip Kaggle upload when page range set; background extract; disk cache; optional Kaggle CPU extract+regex without Llama.

**Dev defaults (2026-08-17):** `EXTRACT_PROVIDER=local`, `CHAPTERWISE_TOPIC_BUILDER=regex`, `TEXT_PROVIDER=azure` (`gpt-4.1-mini` via `AZURE_CHAT_*`), `CHAPTERWISE_TEXT_EXTRACTOR=rapidocr`, `CHAPTERWISE_DEFER_IMAGE_B64=1` (code default), TTS voice **`shimmer`**, decorative gpt-image-2 **on-demand only**. Kaggle is optional. Notebook LLM defaults if used: `MAX_NEW_TOKENS=512`, `MAX_TIME_SECONDS=90`, `CHAT_JOB_MAX_SECONDS=120`.
